A||||6||86SE||Wont Start!!||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||03-20-2000||05:34 PM||||The other day I filled up at the gas station and the car stalled.  After a few hours the car fired up again.  I drove it for another 40 miles with about 4 restarts and everythings OK.  This morning I try to start it and it just turns over and over and over without starting.  Another guy with the same type of problem says I should replace the ignition coil.  <P>I know its gettin fuel because a can smell it all around the car and from the exhaust tips. <P>So nows the question, do I go out and buy a coil and hope it clears up the problem, or does the problem lie elsewhere???<P>THANKS!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||william_thorniii||03-20-2000||07:02 PM||||86,<P>Sounds like the coil to me.  Since the coils go out regularly on our little cars, it is just as well you have a spare anyway... but if you really want to check out the coil idea.  You could check and see if it is firing at all by grounding it to the block.  Be careful, these newer ignitions pack more of a punch than older ones.  You will get shocked if you are not smart (read: you will get shocked if you are like me).  This is not sure fire since it will not determine if the coil is putting out enough juice.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000002||86SE||03-20-2000||07:11 PM||||alright thanks!  i went out and bought one and now i have to put it on.<P>86SE||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||03-20-2000||10:23 PM||||Put the new coil in and she fired right up!!||||reg||14
Z||000004||Luperman||03-20-2000||10:25 PM||||you might also invest in a new ignition module it would have the same symptoms , when it would get hot it would stop working and you would have to wait until it cools down some to start firing again.||||reg||5
Z||000005||fiero56||03-20-2000||10:51 PM||||Coil or iginition module can be checked for free at most auto parts places. I took mine to AutoZone since they can test out of car for free(very nice service). I can attest to these systems putting out some juice. I had no idea spark would ground through me THAT well from a plug boot. Watch out for those really old magneto systems too, ouch.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shiner||03-21-2000||12:32 AM||||Back when I was learning to set the ignition timing on my '84 SC, I shocked myself three, yes three, times.  The first time I suprised the crap out of me, but the other times felt kind of good.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
